 fingers form the kangaroo’s ears and nose.","source_url":"https://www.umkc.edu/about/traditions.html?mobilesearchterms=2025","source_title":"UMKC Traditions","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The university says Roo Up appears across campus and at sporting events.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"umkc-alma-mater","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"UMKC Alma Mater","title":"Join the alma mater","subtitle":"A song first sung to the Men’s Glee Club in 1940","notes":"Learn the refrain before a home sporting event and sing with the crowd. The words celebrate UMKC’s blue and gold and connect today’s Roos with earlier classes.","short_summary":"A 1940 school song still sung at UMKC home sporting events.","evidence_claim":"UMKC states that its alma mater was first sung to the Men’s Glee Club in 1940 and is sung at all UMKC home sporting events.","source_url":"https://www.umkc.edu/about/traditions.html?mobilesearchterms=2025","source_title":"UMKC Traditions","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"UMKC says the alma mater is sung at all home sporting events.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"umkc-old-gold-and-royal-blue","subject_type":"tradition","entity_name":"Old Gold and Royal Blue","title":"Wear the school colors","subtitle":"Student council chose the palette in 1934","notes":"Choose Roo blue and gold for a campus event or photo. The color pairing is a student-established part of UMKC identity, reaching back to the university’s early years.","short_summary":"UMKC’s official colors have been old gold and royal blue since 1934.","evidence_claim":"UMKC says the student council named “old gold and royal blue” the official school colors in 1934 and that they remain in u